To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the New York Freedom of Information Law, I hereby request the following records:

, I request existing electronic reports, spreadsheets, tracking logs, and collection-agency reports concerning NYC Health + Hospitals patient accounts placed with third-party collection agencies that were recalled, closed, adjusted, refunded, or otherwise corrected from January 1, 2021, through December 31, 2025, because of:

    Duplicate charges or duplicate billing;

    Duplicate payments;

    Prior patient or insurer payment;

    Incorrect patient responsibility; or

    Other billing errors.

Please provide existing monthly, quarterly, annual, or appropriately de-identified account-level records showing, where maintained:

    Collection-agency name;

    Hospital or facility name;

    Placement date and correction, recall, or closure date;

    Recall or adjustment reason code and description;

    Number of affected accounts, for aggregate reports;

    Original balance placed for collection;

    Amount collected before correction, recall, or closure;

    Amount remitted to the hospital;

    Amount refunded to the patient or other payer;

    Amount reversed, credited, adjusted, or written off;

    Agency fee or commission associated with the affected accounts; and

    Refund or correction status, including outstanding amounts if maintained.

Please also provide existing:

    Data dictionaries and documentation defining the reason codes and financial fields;

    Policies or procedures governing how billing corrections are communicated to collection agencies and how refunds or account recalls are processed; and

    Reports or audits concerning duplicate billing, collection of previously paid balances, or failure to stop collection after a billing correction.

I do not seek patient names, account numbers, addresses, dates of birth, medical-record numbers, diagnoses, or other individually identifying health information. Please redact exempt information and release reasonably segregable nonexempt portions.

If account-level records cannot be released, please provide existing aggregate reports covering the requested categories. I am not requesting creation of a new report or analysis.

Please provide tabular records in their existing electronic format, preferably CSV or XLSX, and release available records on a rolling basis. If any portion is withheld, please identify the applicable statutory exemption.

Please contact me before incurring fees exceeding $25.

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 5 business days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

Cristina Alvarez

To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the New York Freedom of Information Law, I hereby request the following records:

I request existing electronic complaint logs, case-management exports, tracking spreadsheets, and summary reports held by the Health Care Bureau and Consumer Frauds and Protection Bureau concerning duplicate medical billing and related medical-debt collection complaints received from January 1, 2021, through December 31, 2025.

Please include complaints categorized or otherwise identified as involving:

    Duplicate charges or duplicate billing for the same medical service;

    Requests for payment or collection of medical balances already paid by a patient or insurer;

    Duplicate payments or payments exceeding the amount owed;

    The same medical debt pursued by multiple collectors; or

    Collection activity continuing after a duplicate charge or billing error was corrected.

For responsive complaints, please provide the following fields, where maintained:

    Non-identifying complaint or case identifier;

    Date received and date closed;

    Hospital, provider, insurer, collection agency, and original creditor named;

    Complaint category, subcategory, issue code, and redacted issue description;

    Case status, disposition, and resolution;

    Amount disputed or alleged to have been billed in duplicate;

    Amount reported paid by the consumer;

    Amount refunded, credited, canceled, or otherwise adjusted;

    Restitution or savings recorded by the office, including any separately maintained distinction between refunds and avoided charges;

    Whether a duplicate charge or billing error was acknowledged or confirmed, if recorded; and

    Referral or enforcement outcome, if maintained.

If this request is denied in whole or in part, please provide a written explanation identifying the specific statutory exemption relied upon and explaining its application to the records withheld. Please also provide instructions for appealing the determination.

If responsive records contain exempt information, please redact only the exempt portions and disclose all reasonably segregable nonexempt portions. Please identify the statutory basis for any redactions when providing the records. You do not need to obtain my approval before making legally required redactions.

Please contact me if any aspect of this request requires clarification, including the scope, technical specifications, available data fields, or electronic format. If clarification or narrowing would facilitate disclosure, I welcome that discussion before a denial.

My telephone number is (714) 747-7935. For clarification questions, I prefer telephone communication rather than postal mail. Please also document any substantive clarification, fee estimate, or determination in this MuckRock request’s correspondence thread.

I am requesting these records for journalistic reporting on duplicate medical billing and related debt-collection practices. Because the information is of timely public interest, I would appreciate processing as promptly as practicable and disclosure of available records on a rolling basis.

Please provide the initial response required by New York FOIL within five business days of receipt: disclosure of the records, a written denial, or a written acknowledgment with an approximate date for granting or denying the request.

Thank you for your assistance

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 5 business days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

Cristina Alvarez
